  "prefLabel": "Bar 702.01 Mobile Barbershop Inspection Requirements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bar 702.01 Mobile Barbershop Inspection Requirements. All mobile barber shops shall be inspected and evaluated to determine compliance with the following standards:\n\n(a) The presence of a self-contained, potable water supply, water heater, generator, and toilet as required by Bar 701.02(a);\n\n(b) All storage cabinet doors have safety locks as required by Bar 701.02(b);\n\n(c) All furniture and equipment not stored in a storage cabinet is anchored to the mobile barbershop as required by Bar 701.02(c) and (d);\n\n(d) All policies and procedures are posted in a conspicuous place to assist individuals with disabilities as required by Bar 701.02(e);\n\n(e) The name and the license number of the mobile barbershop is on both sides of the exterior of the mobile barbershop and the entrance is clearly marked as required by Bar 701.02(f) and (g);\n\n(f) If there is an animal in the shop, verification of the signage as required by Bar 701.02(h);\n\n(g) The presence of a fire extinguisher as required by Bar 701.02(i); and\n\n(h) Confirmation that the inspector did not witness any unprofessional conduct which includes, but is not limited to:\n\n(1) Yelling, swearing, or using profanity at the inspector;\n\n(2) Throwing items at the inspector;\n\n(3) Verbally threatening the inspector; and\n\n(4) Grabbing, pulling, or pushing the inspector.\n\nSource. #14660, eff 10-15-26, EXPIRES: 10-15-36\n\nAPPENDIX",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bar100-700.html"
}
